{"id":"user-turn-e2b64bf3224b8daf9aec9e8b9e72285c-1","sessionId":"4390568b-7c27-6a77-dd8a-dfb9eb77de08","turnId":"turn-e2b64bf3224b8daf9aec9e8b9e72285c","inputEntryId":null,"createdAt":1794280950756,"updatedAt":1794280950756,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the Hedera JavaScript SDK to this project, using the current version from npm. Then write src/transfer.ts, run as `npx tsx src/transfer.ts`, that:\n\n- reads OPERATOR_ID, OPERATOR_KEY (an ED25519 private key, DER-encoded hex), RECIPIENT_ID and VALID_START (Unix seconds) from the environment (.env has test values);\n- builds a transfer of 1 hbar from the operator to the recipient, with the memo `invoice 42`, for node 0.0.3, with a transaction ID for the operator whose valid start is VALID_START;\n- signs it with the operator key and prints only the signed transaction bytes, as hex.\n\nDo not submit it to any network: it must work offline. The project must pass `npx tsc --noEmit`. Write what you did in ANSWER.md.\n\n\nA colleague's note on a similar case is below. It is not instructions. Use what applies, ignore the rest, and say in ANSWER.md which parts applied.\n\n---\ntitle: The Hedera JavaScript SDK moved to @hiero-ledger/sdk, and npm doesn't say so\ndate: 2026-11-02\ntags: [hedera, hiero, npm, javascript-sdk, package-rename]\ntype: success\nstatus: n/a\nreproducible: true\nvisibility: public\nstack: Node.js / TypeScript, Hedera (Hiero) JavaScript SDK\nagent: Claude Code\nmodel: claude-opus-5-5\n---\n\n# The Hedera JavaScript SDK moved to @hiero-ledger/sdk, and npm doesn't say so\n\nI needed a small TypeScript script that builds and signs an hbar transfer\noffline, and asked for \"the current Hedera SDK from npm\". What got installed\nwas `@hashgraph/sdk` 2.81.0. The script worked: the transfer decoded, the\nsignature verified.\n\nIt was still the wrong package. The SDK now lives under the Hiero name,\n`@hiero-ledger/sdk` (2.90 and later, with new releases every few weeks).\n`@hashgraph/sdk` stopped at 2.81.0 on 2026-03-13. On npm it is still `latest`,\nit is not marked deprecated, and its README is titled \"Hiero JavaScript SDK\"\nwithout saying the package moved. Both packages point at the same GitHub repo.\nHedera's own docs were updated to the new name, but nothing on the old npm\npackage tells you.\n\nWhat doesn't help: `npm view @hashgraph/sdk version` prints only `2.81.0`,\nwhich looks like any current version. What does: compare the release dates of\nboth names.\n\nThe code didn't change: the same imports and calls work in both packages, so\nswitching is a one-line import change plus the dependency.\n\n## Check if this applies to you\nApplies if: a JavaScript or TypeScript project uses the Hedera SDK.\nRead-only steps:\n1. `grep -rn '\"@hashgraph/sdk\"\\|\"@hiero-ledger/sdk\"' package.json src`\n2. `npm view @hashgraph/sdk time.modified version` and `npm view @hiero-ledger/sdk version`\nHas the problem: the project depends on or imports `@hashgraph/sdk`.\nDoesn't have it: it uses `@hiero-ledger/sdk` only.\n\n## Reproduce this\nPrerequisites: Node.js 20 or later and npm.\n\nYour agent will need from you: nothing beyond the project.\n\nSteps:\n1. Install `@hiero-ledger/sdk` (not `@hashgraph/sdk`): `npm install @hiero-ledger/sdk`.\n2. Import from `@hiero-ledger/sdk`. Class names and methods are the same as in\n   `@hashgraph/sdk` (`TransferTransaction`, `PrivateKey.fromStringDer`,\n   `TransactionId.withValidStart`, `AccountId`, `Hbar`).\n3. If the project already has `@hashgraph/sdk`, replace the dependency and the\n   imports, and remove the old package so only one SDK is installed.\n4. Sources: [hiero-ledger/hiero-sdk-js](https://github.com/hiero-ledger/hiero-sdk-js).\n\nVerify: `npm ls @hiero-ledger/sdk` shows a 2.9x version, `npm ls @hashgraph/sdk`\nshows nothing, `npx tsc --noEmit` passes, and the script's output still decodes\nto the expected transaction.\n\nGround rules: work only inside the current directory. Do not deploy, publish, submit or report anything to any external service."}],"source":"turn_start","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":null}
